.Dd $Mdocdate: September 4 2026 $
.Dt PLDOCK 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pldock
.Nd swallow X clients into a Perl X11 dock rectangle
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm pldock
.Op Fl v
.Op Fl c Ar file
.Op Fl screen Ar output
.Op Fl pos Ar place
.Op Fl top | Fl bottom
.Op Fl height Ar pixels
.Op Fl gap Ar pixels
.Op Fl override | Fl managed
.Op Fl spawn
.Op Fl no-clock
.Op Fl no-apm
.Op Fl no-load
.Op Fl no-console
.Op Fl h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
creates one dark X11 rectangle and
.Em swallows
already-mapped clients into it using Perl
.Nm X11::Protocol .
It is a small Perl dock in the same style as xtomato's
.Nm plxmessage :
no toolkit.
Default swallow tiles are
.Nm wmclock ,
.Nm wmapm ,
.Nm xload ,
and
.Nm xconsole .
A
.Ic plugin
line in
.Xr pldock.conf 1
opens a child window owned by
.Nm
instead of swallowing a foreign client; see
.Ic xloadio
there.
.Pp
Geometry is relative to one
.Xr xrandr 1
output, not the combined virtual desktop.
The default layout is the lower-right corner of the primary output,
with
.Nm xconsole
along the bottom and the other three tiled in a row above it.
See
.Xr pldock.conf 1 .
.Pp
.Nm
does not
.Xr fork 2
or
.Xr execve 2
clients unless
.Fl spawn
is given or the config contains
.Ic spawn .
Matching uses
.Dv WM_CLASS
and
.Dv WM_NAME ,
including the last path component, so a class of
.Pa /usr/local/bin/wmapm
matches tile
.Ic wmapm .
.Pp
The dock is a normal managed window by default so
.Xr cwm 1
can select and cycle it.
.Fl override
makes it override-redirect
.Pq cwm will not select it; placement is pinned .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c Ar file
Read layout from
.Ar file
instead of the search path below.
.It Fl screen Ar output
Place the dock on this
.Xr xrandr 1
output:
.Ic primary ,
an output name
.Pq e.g. HDMI-1 ,
.Ic left ,
.Ic right ,
or a 0-based index.
.It Fl pos Ar place
Corner on that output:
.Ic top-left ,
.Ic top-right ,
.Ic bottom-left ,
.Ic bottom-right .
.It Fl top
Same as
.Fl pos Ar top-right .
.It Fl bottom
Same as
.Fl pos Ar bottom-right .
.It Fl height Ar pixels
Dock height.
Default is
.Ic auto
from the tile tree.
.It Fl gap Ar pixels
Gap between cells
.Pq default 2 .
.It Fl override
Override-redirect.
.Xr cwm 1
cannot select or cycle the dock.
.It Fl managed
Normal managed window
.Pq default .
.It Fl spawn
.Xr fork 2 Ns / Ns Xr exec 3
any tile that is not already mapped.
.It Fl v , Fl verbose
Log each xrandr output, the dock rectangle, and every ingest attempt
by name
.Pq looking for, found, ingested, or not found .
.It Fl no-clock , Fl no-apm , Fl no-load , Fl no-console
Skip that tile.
.It Fl h , Fl help
Print usage to standard error.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width PLDOCK_CONF
.It Ev DISPLAY
Required.
.Nm
exits if it is unset or empty; it never defaults a display.
.It Ev PLDOCK_CONF
Config path, used if
.Fl c
is not given.
.El
.Sh SIGNALS
.Bl -tag -width SIGTERM
.It Dv SIGINT , Dv SIGTERM
Reparent swallowed clients back to the root at their saved position and
size, destroy the dock, and exit.
Clients are not killed.
.It Dv SIGHUP
The same spit, then re-read the config, recreate the rectangle, and
ingest again.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width ~/.config/pldock/pldock.conf -compact
.It Pa ~/.config/pldock/pldock.conf
Default config.
.Fl c
and
.Ev PLDOCK_CONF
override it.
The current directory is not searched.
.El
.Pp
If that file does not exist, a built-in copy of the default layout is used.
An example is installed as
.Pa /usr/local/share/examples/pldock/pldock.conf .
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
pldock
pldock -v -screen HDMI-1
pldock -c ~/pldock.conf -override
kill -HUP $(pgrep -f pldock)
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cwm 1 ,
.Xr pldock.conf 1 ,
.Xr wmapm 1 ,
.Xr wmclock 1 ,
.Xr xconsole 1 ,
.Xr xload 1 ,
.Xr xrandr 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Todd T. Fries Aq Mt todd@fries.net
